-- title:
--   Two q-expansion readings and a retraction on the j-chart ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$; assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` (namely $q^{-1}$ times the rational coefficient image of the integral series `jNum`) lies in the subfield `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms with integral $q$-expansions. Write $\mathcal{O}_M$ and $\mathcal{O}_N$ for the $j$-finite chart algebras `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj` and `chartAlgFin p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj`, i.e. the subalgebras of elements of the respective $q$-expansion function fields integral over the subalgebra generated over the base ring `R p` by the chosen $j$-element. Given an `R p`-algebra map $\iota_0 : \mathcal{O}_N \to \mathcal{O}_M$ preserving $q$-expansions as Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, an `R p`-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $\mathcal{O}_M$ with $\theta(\iota_0 b)$ having $q$-expansion `qExpand ℚ p` of that of $b$ (substitution $q \mapsto q^p$), a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ and algebraically closed, and a ring map $\rho : R p \to A$ compatible with the structure map $R p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, then, with $\kappa$ an `R p`-algebra via the residue map composed with $\rho$, there exist ring homomorphisms $\theta_0, \theta_1 : \mathcal{O}_M \to \kappa((q))$ and a $\kappa$-algebra map $\sigma_0 : \kappa \otimes_{R p} \mathcal{O}_M \to \kappa \otimes_{R p} \mathcal{O}_N$ such that: $\theta_1 = \theta_0 \circ \theta$; whenever $y \in A((q))$ pushes forward along $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to the image of the rational $q$-expansion of $c$, one has $\theta_0(c)$ equal to the coefficientwise residue of $y$; $\ker\theta_0 \ne \ker\theta_1$ and the minimal primes over the ideal $(p)$ of $\mathcal{O}_M$ are exactly $\ker\theta_0$ and $\ker\theta_1$; $\theta_0(\theta(\iota_0 b)) = \theta_0(\iota_0 b)^p =$ `qExpand κ p` $(\theta_0(\iota_0 b))$ for all $b \in \mathcal{O}_N$; $\sigma_0$ is surjective and retracts $\mathrm{id}_\kappa \otimes \iota_0$; the minimal primes of $\kappa \otimes_{R p} \mathcal{O}_M$ are exactly $\ker\sigma_0$ and its preimage under $\mathrm{id}_\kappa \otimes \theta$, and these two are distinct; and $\sigma_0(1 \otimes c) = 0$ if and only if $\theta_0(c) = 0$.
--
--   This is the algebraic form, on the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model, of the Deligne–Rapoport description of the fibre at $p$ of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(M)$ with $p$ exactly dividing $M$: two components, each a copy of the curve of level $M/p$, distinguished by reading $q$-expansions in $q$ and in $q^p$, corresponding to the two minimal primes of the fibre ring. It is obtained by combining the construction of the pair of $q$-expansion readings, the construction of the retraction onto the lower-level chart ring, and the count of minimal primes of the geometric fibre; downstream it supplies the closed-immersion and minimal-prime data used to analyse the components of the special fibre.
